Usage:
  x2c build [options] <input>...
  x2c build [options] [--target <name>]

Translate x2c sources, compile C sources, and link one target.
With explicit inputs, the default target is an executable. Without
inputs, x2c reads the nearest x2c.toml and builds its default
target.

Target options:
      --manifest-path <file>  Use <file> instead of discovering x2c.toml
      --target <name>         Build the named manifest target
      --profile <name>        Apply the named manifest build profile
      --kind <kind>           executable or static-library
  -c, --compile-only          Produce object files without linking
  -j, --jobs <count>          Maximum parallel translation and compilation jobs

Output options:
      --output <file>         Name the executable, library, or single object
      --build-dir <dir>       Store generated C, objects, deps, and state here
      --save-temps[=<dir>]    Keep generated C and other intermediate files

Translation options:
  -I <dir>                    Add a shared x2c/C include directory
      --x-include-dir <dir>   Add an x2c-only include directory
      --c-include-dir <dir>   Add a C-only ordinary include directory
      --c-system-dir <dir>    Add a C-only system include directory
      --package-dir <dir>     Add a directory of x2c packages
      --no-cpp                Skip symbol collection and preprocessing
      --live-symbols          Collect symbols through the host preprocessor
      --cpp-symbols           Use CPP collection for this translation

C compiler options:
      --cc <program>          Use <program> as the host C compiler
      --ar <program>          Use <program> as the static-library archiver
  -O0, -O1, -O2, -O3, -Os     Set C optimization
  -g                          Emit debug information
  -D <name>[=<value>]         Define a C preprocessor macro
  -U <name>                   Undefine a C preprocessor macro
  -Xcc <arg>                  Pass one argument only to C compilation

Linker options:
  -L <dir>                    Add a library search directory
  -l <name>                   Link library <name>
  -Wl,<arg>[,<arg>...]        Pass comma-separated arguments to the linker
  -Xlinker <arg>              Pass one argument to the linker

General options:
  -h, --help                  Show help and exit
  -v, --verbose               Show commands as they are executed
  -###                        Show commands without executing them
  -q, --quiet                 Suppress successful progress and receipts
      --plain                 Use stable output without terminal rendering
      --color <auto|always|never>
                              Control terminal color
      --debug                 Enable compiler debug logging
  @<file>                     Read additional arguments from a response file
  --                          End option parsing

Inputs may be .x, .c, .o, or .a files. x2c links its runtime and
required platform libraries automatically. Directory operands and
unexpanded wildcard operands are rejected.
